    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. My main concern is that some of the assets were tucked away in accounts that weren't easily visible during the first audit. If HMRC finds these \"hidden\" items later, how aggressive are they usually with the penalties? Also, are there any specific ways they go about sniffing out these kinds of discrepancies in foreign accounts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "HMRC's approach to penalties is typically dependent on the intent behind the omission; accidental oversight is treated much less severely than deliberate concealment. They utilize sophisticated international databases, agreements like the Common Reporting Standard (CRS), and cooperation from foreign tax authorities to track assets held abroad. If they uncover undeclared assets, the penalties can range from interest charges to substantial fines based on the value of the undeclared assets.",
      "source": "target",
